# Destination allowlist for the egress proxy (extended regex, anchored). Matched
# against the requested host (HTTP) or CONNECT host (HTTPS, SSH tunnels).
#
# This proxy is the agent's ONLY path out: its networks are `internal` with no
# gateway (docker-compose.yml), so a host that is not listed here is unreachable,
# not merely filtered. One line, one reason. Site additions go in
# site/proxy-filter.extra, appended at build; the forge and the notification push
# host belong there, not here.
#
# The Anthropic relay: model requests, feature flags, Remote Control.
^api\.anthropic\.com$
# claude.ai account login and the OAuth token exchange/refresh behind it
# (code.claude.com/docs/en/network-config). The refresh runs monthly without
# a human; blocking platform.claude.com makes the credential die silently.
^claude\.ai$
^platform\.claude\.com$
# GitHub: git over HTTPS and SSH (CONNECT :22), the REST API, Actions checks.
^github\.com$
^api\.github\.com$
# Package registries. PyPI and npm are CDN-fronted with rotating IPs, which
# is why hostname matching is the control here.
^pypi\.org$
^files\.pythonhosted\.org$
^[a-z0-9.-]+\.pythonhosted\.org$
^registry\.npmjs\.org$
